From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:33:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake,mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: C1E and C-state
 auto-demotion

FSP-S enables Enhanced C1 and the C1 and C3 auto-demotion and
un-demotion by default (its C1e, C1StateAutoDemotion, C1StateUnDemotion,
C3StateAutoDemotion and C3StateUnDemotion), and the Lenovo firmware of
the M720q, M920q and M920x, which runs its CPU init through FSP, has
them on ("C-State Auto Demotion: C1 and C3"). coreboot does the CPU
init itself on Cannon Lake and left them off: MSR_POWER_CTL bit 1 and
bits 25-28 of MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL were 0 on an M920x.

Add the devicetree options c1e_enable and cstate_auto_demotion, off by
default, set in the same writes as the locks of these MSRs on every
core, and turn both on for these boards. Package C-state demotion stays
off, as there.

TEST=On the M920x with the i3-8100 (ci-169 against ci-170): MSR 0xE2
0x00008008 before, 0x1e008008 after on every core; idle (30 s) 0.57
and 0.54 W, PC9 85.8% both; 60 s on all cores 44.64 and 44.50 W,
stable. Under Linux, MSR_POWER_CTL bit 1 still reads 0: intel_idle
turns C1E promotion off on this processor and asks for C1E itself, so
c1e_enable matters for the other OSes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb | 5 +++++
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h                | 7 +++++++
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c                 | 5 +++++
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 4a83c3401f..1f11aba3f5 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -24,6 +24,11 @@ chip soc/intel/cannonlake
 	# values for it. 0, the default, keeps the generic values of FSP-S
 	register "VrPowerDeliveryDesign" = "11"
 
+	# C1E and the C1/C3 auto-demotion and un-demotion, as the OEM firmware
+	# (Intel's defaults there, through FSP-S)
+	register "c1e_enable" = "true"
+	register "cstate_auto_demotion" = "true"
+
 	# Wake on LAN from S4 and S5, as the OEM firmware (the "wake_on_lan" option)
 	register "WolEnableOverride" = "true"
 
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
index 27be8f1abd..7bf31a241a 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
@@ -253,6 +253,13 @@ struct soc_intel_cannonlake_config {
 	bool TetonGlacierMode;
 
 	bool eist_enable;
+	/*
+	 * Enhanced C1 (C1E: MSR_POWER_CTL bit 1) and the C1 and C3 auto-demotion
+	 * and un-demotion of MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL (bits 25-28), which FSP-S
+	 * would enable by default but coreboot's CPU init leaves off
+	 */
+	bool c1e_enable;
+	bool cstate_auto_demotion;
 	bool enable_c6dram;
 
 	/*
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
index ed211e011a..0c9bcaf05e 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@ static void configure_misc(void)
 	msr = rdmsr(MSR_POWER_CTL);
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 0);	/* Enable Bi-directional PROCHOT as an input */
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 18);	/* Enable Energy/Performance Bias control */
+	if (conf->c1e_enable)
+		msr.lo |= POWER_CTL_C1E_MASK;	/* Enhanced C1 */
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 23);	/* Lock it */
 	wrmsr(MSR_POWER_CTL, msr);
 }
@@ -83,6 +85,9 @@ static void configure_c_states(const config_t *const cfg)
 	if (cfg->max_package_c_state && (msr.lo & 0xf) >= cfg->max_package_c_state) {
 		msr.lo = (msr.lo & ~0xf) | ((cfg->max_package_c_state - 1) & 0xf);
 	}
+	/* C3 and C1 auto-demotion (bits 25, 26) and un-demotion (27, 28) */
+	if (cfg->cstate_auto_demotion)
+		msr.lo |= (1 << 25) | (1 << 26) | (1 << 27) | (1 << 28);
 	/*
 	 * CFG Lock, which locks bits 15:0 until the next reset: the "cfg_lock"
 	 * option, on by default. macOS writes this MSR, and with the lock it
-- 
2.47.3

